<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antiochus VII Sidetes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 129 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antiochus VII Sidetes was a Seleucid king who attempted to restore the dynasty's power in the second century BCE. He launched a major campaign to recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and the east from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a> but was defeated and killed in 129 BCE. His death ended Seleucid hopes of regaining the eastern provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antiochus-vii-sidetes.jpg" alt="Antiochus VII Sidetes" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Antiochus_VII_Euergetes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
